  "reason": "Under Fla. Stat. s. 83.49(3)(a), if the landlord does not intend to impose a claim on the security deposit, the landlord must return it within 15 days, not 30 days. The reference answer misstates this period as 30 days.",
  "verdict": "dispute",
  "issues": [
    "wrong_number_or_date"
  ],
  "proposed_fix": "No. Under Fla. Stat. s. 83.49(3)(a), if the landlord does not intend to claim any of the deposit, he must return it within 15 days after the rental agreement ends. If he intends to claim part of it, he must give the tenant written notice of the claim and its reason within 30 days after the agreement ends, by certified mail or by e-mail under s. 83.505, or he forfeits the right to impose the claim. Sixty days without any notice misses both statutory deadlines."
}
